  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =((-1,0)\\cup (0,2))\\times (1,3) \\\\  & =((-1,0)\\times (1,3))\\cup ((0,2)\\times (1,3)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{(-1,0)\\times (1,3)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{(0,2)\\times (1,3)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{(-1,0)\\times (1,3)}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{(0,2)\\times (1,3)}2\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
